{
  "description": "Golden vector for the DoctorDO signed-request protocol v1 (ADR-0029). Verifiers must VERIFY the signatures; ECDSA signatures are randomised, so implementations must not compare their own signature bytes for ECDSA. RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 is deterministic: an implementation signing the RSA canonical string with the RSA key must produce exactly the signature given. The keys are throwaway test keys.",
  "protocol": {
    "canonicalString": "Lines joined by a single LF, no trailing newline: \"DOCTORDO-SIG-1\", method, path, host, x-doctordo-kind, x-doctordo-collected-at, x-doctordo-signed-at, x-doctordo-nonce, base64(SHA-256(body bytes as sent)). UTF-8. Header values are used exactly as sent.",
    "host": "The verifier uses its configured public ingest host (lower case, no port), never the request Host header. The collector uses the host of its configured ingest URI.",
    "signedAt": "RFC 3339 UTC with Z and whole seconds. Accepted within plus or minus 300 seconds of the verifier clock.",
    "nonce": "16 random bytes, base64url without padding (22 characters). Not reused within the acceptance window.",
    "deviceCert": "Leaf certificate DER, standard base64 with padding.",
    "signature": "Standard base64 with padding. The algorithm follows the certificate key type: RSA uses RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 with SHA-256; EC P-256 uses ECDSA with SHA-256 in IEEE P1363 (r||s) form, which is what .NET ECDsa.SignData returns."
  },
